# Grok Bot Agent Factory Rules

This repository follows the **Grok Bot Agent Factory** autonomous workflow. Read `AGENTS.md` and `.factory/config.json` before acting.

## 0. Working Repository Creation & Bootstrap (`template init`)
- New working repositories created from this template MUST be created as **PUBLIC** (`gh repo create <name> --public --template cesarchavezcal/grok-bot-agent-factory --clone`) so GitHub Free allows branch protection (`ci` required check) and auto-merge (`allow_auto_merge`).
- Run `./scripts/init.sh` (idempotent) to install/verify locked skills, create labels (`agent`, `epic`, `deploy`, `bug`, etc.), configure merge policy, and protect `main`.

## 1. Intake Gate & Skill Routing (`agent`, `bug`, `epic` Labels)
- Process **only** GitHub Issues or Linear Issues carrying the `agent` label. Ignore all other issues.
- **Routing Matrix & Precedence**:
  - **`epic` + `agent`** -> **`plan-epic`**: Planning-only thread that decomposes an epic into vertical sub-issues (`Part of #N`). Every created sub-issue MUST get the `agent` label; exactly one final sub-issue gets the `deploy` label. Verify all sub-issues have `agent` before ending. Epics stay planning-only (no build).
    - *Precedence*: `epic` takes priority over all other labels. If an issue carries `epic` + `bug` + `agent`, it routes to `plan-epic`.
  - **`bug` + `agent`** -> **`fix-bug`**: Starts with short plan in thread. Read issue/error/logs -> reproduce first (if cannot reproduce or open questions, stop and ask in thread final message; if no questions, write "No questions, starting build" and build immediately in same run) -> write failing test -> fix root cause (`ce-debug`, `tdd`, `principle-fix-root-causes`) -> verify all tests + run app once -> Grok audit -> PR `Closes #N` -> squash merge on green.
  - **`agent` alone (or with `feature`)** -> **`implement-ticket`**: Starts with short plan in thread. If questions, stop and ask in thread final message; if no questions, write "No questions, starting build" and continue to build in same run -> plan (`grill-with-docs` + `wayfinder`) -> build (`poteto-mode` reproduce, test, fix, verify) -> Grok audit -> rework rule -> PR `Closes #N` -> squash merge on green CI.
- **Manual Labeling Order (`epic` before `agent`)**:
  - When manually adding labels to an existing issue in GitHub or Linear, **always add `epic` before `agent`** so `epic` is already present on the issue payload when `agent` triggers `.github/workflows/notify-grok.yml`.
- **Deploy Rule**:
  - Deploy only on the last sub-issue of an epic (carrying the `deploy` label), after its green merge.
  - Intermediate sub-issues never deploy.
- **Issue Closing**: Every PR body MUST include `Closes #N` (never `Refs #N`) so the issue closes when the PR merges; for epics, the final deploy sub-issue PR also includes `Closes #EPIC`. Agents never close issues by hand.
- Track active work in `.factory/work-items/<id>.json` (conforming to `.factory/work-item.schema.json`). Do not commit runtime work-item instances unless requested.

## 2. Workflow & Agent-Run Rules (Plan-Then-Build & GitHub Account)
- **Plan-Then-Build**:
  - Every issue thread starts with a short plan in the thread (files, tests, verification).
  - If there is ANY open question, ask it in the thread and stop without editing files. Wait for the human answer, then build.
  - If there are NO questions, write `"No questions, starting build"` and continue to the build in the same run (no waiting for a separate build message).
  - Epics (`epic` label) stay planning-only: create the `agent` sub-issues, no build.
  - Keep all existing gates: PR with `Closes #N`, Grok audit, squash-merge only when `ci` is green AND the audit passes, deploy only for the `deploy` sub-issue.
- **GitHub Account Rule (`cesarchavezcal`)**:
  - Every commit, push, and PR must use the `cesarchavezcal` account.
  - Check `gh auth status` first before any push or `gh` command. If the active account is not `cesarchavezcal`, remember the active account, switch using `gh auth switch --user cesarchavezcal`, and switch back to the earlier account when done.
  - Maintain git email `cesarchavezcal@gmail.com` via `includeIf`, never changing the global git email.

## 3. Communication Rules (Zero Issue/PR Comments)
- **NEVER comment on issues or PRs**.
- When a bug cannot be reproduced, or when grilling/clarification is needed for César:
  1. Deduce everything possible from the codebase, tests, and existing docs first.
  2. If genuine ambiguities or reproduction blockers remain, stop execution immediately.
  3. Write the numbered questions or reproduction block directly in the **thread final message**.
  4. The external dispatcher (**Grok Bot**) relays the message to César. Do NOT post a GitHub/Linear comment or add a `waiting-for-human` comment.

## 4. Build, Verification & Merge
- Building runs exclusively through official pstack `/poteto-mode` (`.agents/skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md`) using the **`Autopilot-full`** playbook (`.agents/skills/poteto-mode/playbooks/autopilot-full.md`) and seam-first [`tdd`](.agents/skills/tdd/SKILL.md).
- **Max Concurrency**: `3` isolated Git worktrees off `main` in parallel (never stacked).
- **Proof & Merge Gate**:
  1. Green CI check (`ci`).
  2. Independent runtime verification via `.agents/skills/verify-app` (or `verify-<app>`) with `exitCode === 0`.
  3. Independent cross-model adversarial interrogation on `grok::grok-4.7` (`reasoningEffort: "high"`) returning `PASS`.
- **Squash Merge (Never Delete Branches)**:
  - Merge using `gh pr merge <PR_NUMBER> --squash`.
  - **Strict Rule**: NEVER pass `--delete-branch`. Never delete branches.

## 5. Model Routing & Rework Escalation (Zero API Keys, Zero Claude, Zero Argon)
- **Scout**: `antigravity::gemini-3.8-flash-low` (`AGY_FAST`, low effort).
- **Spec & Plan**: `antigravity::gemini-3.8-flash-high` (`AGY_FAST`, high effort).
- **UI / CRUD / Standard Build**: `antigravity::gemini-3.8-flash-medium` (`AGY_FAST`, medium effort).
- **Backend / Complex Logic Build** (`db`, `sql`, `concurrency`, `security`, `algorithm`, `state-machine`, `architecture`): `grok-4.7-build-fast` (`GROK_WORK`, `reasoningEffort: medium`).
- **Runtime Verify**: `antigravity::gemini-3.8-flash-medium` (`AGY_FAST`, medium effort).
- **Independent Audit / Interrogation**: `grok::grok-4.7` (`GROK_AUDIT`, `reasoningEffort: "high"`).
- **Rework Escalation**: On verification or audit failure, escalate rework to **`antigravity::gemini-3.8-flash-high`** (`AGY_FAST`, high effort) — strictly distinct from the `grok-4.7` auditor — for a maximum of **2 attempts** (`maxRetries: 2`). Stop and block if still failing after 2 attempts.
- **Task-Based Effort Scaling**:
  - `low` (`gemini-3.8-flash-low`): scout / simple tasks.
  - `medium` (`gemini-3.8-flash-medium`): normal build / verification.
  - `high` (`gemini-3.8-flash-high`): plan / spec / hard build / rework.
- **Invariants**: Never use Claude or GPT models (`disallowClaude: true`), never use Argon models (retired), and never require paid API keys (`strictZeroCost: true`).
